n \tegl_current_window_id = p_window_id;\n+\n+\tif (p_window_id == MAIN_WINDOW_ID) {\n+\t\t// These may have changed if the surface was changed or resized, so grab them again.\n+\t\tegl_display = eglGetCurrentDisplay();\n+\t\tegl_surface = eglGetCurrentSurface(EGL_DRAW);\n+\t\tegl_context = eglGetCurrentContext();\n+\t}","path":"platform/android/display_server_android.cpp","commit_id":"d8eea1ea1c5e87d33762766775c867832e4fc500","original_commit_id":"e9b1c4dad40d7ebcaf661fdd61aac0468ff83f6e","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The problem is that we need to call these on the same thread as `eglMakeCurrent()` was successfully run on. I think those will be invoked on the Java render thread, whereas we need to do this on Godot's render thread, which this function will be run on (and a couple lines up, it should have successfully done the `eglMakeCurrent()` so it should have the correct handles).\r\n\r\nAnyway, I'll double check and see if `notify_surface_changed()` or `reset_window()` run on the correct thread or not.\r\n\r\n(Overall, it would be nice if the Java side could just pass the native EGL handles to us, rather than having to indirectly pass them via `eglMakeCurrent()` and `eglGetCurrent*()`, but we're still using the `javax.microedition.khronos.egl.*` versions of the EGL objects, which don't provide a way to get the native handles out. It looks like the objects on `android.opengl.*` do have a way to do that, though)","created_at":"2025-08-06T13:37:03Z","updated_at":"2025-08-06T15:06:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109080#discussion_r2257179250","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109080","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2257179250"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109080#discussion_r2257179250"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109080"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2257179250/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":1006,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":1010,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2257043325,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":61,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2257301635","pull_request_review_id":3092789858,"id":2257301635,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6Gi7CD","diff_hunk":"@@ -995,4 +1001,11 @@ void DisplayServerAndroid::gl_window_make_current(DisplayServer::WindowID p_wind\n \tERR_FAIL_NULL(godot_java);\n \tgodot_java->make_gl_window_current(p_window_id);\n \tegl_current_window_id = p_window_id;\n+\n+\tif (p_window_id == MAIN_WINDOW_ID) {\n+\t\t// These may have changed if the surface was changed or resized, so grab them again.\n+\t\tegl_display = eglGetCurrentDisplay();\n+\t\tegl_surface = eglGetCurrentSurface(EGL_DRAW);\n+\t\tegl_context = eglGetCurrentContext();\n+\t}","path":"platfor